@startuml

title Secure Introduction: what the store checks before it answers

skinparam shadowing false

start

:receive a challenge request, naming a consumer;
if (is the consumer registered\nand enabled?) then (yes)
  :draw a nonce, record it against the consumer\nwith a short life;
  :answer the nonce, sealed to the consumer's key;
else (no)
  :refuse, as a consumer it does not hold;
  stop
endif

:receive an answer, sealed to the store's key;
if (does it name a nonce this consumer holds,\nunexpired and unused?) then (yes)
  :retire the nonce;
else (no)
  :refuse, as a consumer that proved nothing;
  stop
endif

if (does the consumer own the secret it asks for?) then (yes)
  :seal the secret to the consumer's key;
  :record the act;
  stop
else (no)
  :refuse, as one that holds no such secret;
  stop
endif

@enduml
